# magic-agent — Track 1 spot runtime environment template
#
# Copy to .env in the repo root before running:
#   cp .env.example .env
# NEVER commit .env (it is gitignored). Placeholders only — fill with real values.
#
# FORMAT: this file is consumed VERBATIM by systemd's `EnvironmentFile=` (and by
# `set -a; . .env; set +a` in a shell). Use plain `KEY=value` lines — NO `export`, NO
# quotes, and NO inline comments after a value (systemd treats everything after `=` as
# the value, including a trailing `# note`). Keep every comment on its OWN `#` line.
#
# Run-loop tuning (executor mode, live-data flags, log path) is set via `magic-agent run`
# CLI flags, NOT here. This file holds secrets, credentials, and integration config only.
#
# See docs/track1-spot-runbook.md for the full activation checklist before going live.

# ── Execution mode ──
# The executor is set via the CLI flag `--executor [paper|twak]`.
# Paper is the default and requires NONE of the live secrets below.
# The live loop is: `magic-agent run --executor twak --live-frames --live-cmc`.

# ── LIVE secrets (REQUIRED for `--executor twak`) ──
# build_app(mode="twak") fails closed BEFORE constructing any live port unless ALL six
# of these are present and non-empty (app.py `_require_live_env` / `_LIVE_REQUIRED_ENV`).
# TWAK is the SOLE signer for BSC swaps and CMC x402 payments.
TWAK_ACCESS_ID=your-twak-access-id-placeholder
TWAK_HMAC_SECRET=your-twak-hmac-secret-placeholder
TWAK_WALLET_PASSWORD=your-twak-wallet-password-placeholder
# BSC mainnet JSON-RPC endpoint (receipt polling, confirmation depth, balance reads).
BSC_RPC_URL=https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org
# CoinMarketCap API key — REQUIRED in live (the live universe cannot be fetched without
# it; --live-cmc fails closed when absent). Rank/momentum only — CMC NEVER creates setups.
CMC_API_KEY=your-cmc-api-key-placeholder
# The TWAK wallet address (used for balance reads, RPC, and quote provider).
WALLET_ADDRESS=0xYourWalletAddressPlaceholder

# ── Dashboard / API ──
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE: browser-facing base URL the Next.js dashboard calls for /api/*.
# Served by `magic-agent serve` behind a reverse proxy.
# Example: https://your-domain.example.com/api
# BUILD-TIME: inlined into the web bundle at `npm run build` — set before building
# and rebuild after any change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
